.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-611- *
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-612- * Pi emits a four-line XML block per skill (`<name>`, `<description>`,
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-613- * `<location>`) plus a three-sentence preamble. With 31 skills active in
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-614- * this repo that block measured 13.3 KB — 61.5 % of the total system
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-615- * prompt. The full description text matters when the model has to decide
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:616: * which skill to load, but the model can read SKILL.md on demand: the
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-617- * names alone plus a known location pattern is enough to identify
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-618- * candidates.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-619- *
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-620- * This compressed form preserves:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-621- *   1. The instruction to read SKILL.md when a task matches a skill name.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-622- *   2. The relative-path resolution rule (parent of SKILL.md is the
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-623- *      skill directory).
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-624- *   3. Discoverability of every skill: name + location prefix per skill.
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-625- *
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-626- * It drops:
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts:627: *   - Per-skill description text (model loads it via `read` when a name
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-628- *     matches a task).
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-629- *   - The `<available_skills>` XML envelope and per-skill XML overhead
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-630- *     (~110 bytes per skill of pure structure, plus the location path).
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-631- *
.pi/extensions/pi-cache-optimizer/index.ts-632- * Output shape is a single text block grouped by skill-root directory so
--
